(load "carp-gui.carp")

(Project.config "title" "carp-gui")
(Project.config "docs-directory" "./docs/")
(Project.config "docs-logo" "")
(Project.config "docs-url" "https://github.com/carpentry-org/carp-gui")
(Project.config "docs-styling" "../style.css")
(Project.config "docs-prelude" "An immediate-mode GUI for Carp that emits
WebGPU vertex batches.

```
(load \"git@github.com:carpentry-org/carp-gui@master\")
```

- [`Gui`](./Gui.html) — the widgets and the layout that places them
- [`Context`](./Context.html) — the UI state carried between frames, with
  [`PanelState`](./PanelState.html)
- [`GuiRect`](./GuiRect.html) — rectangles, and the
  [`GuiDrawCommand`](./GuiDrawCommand.html)s they turn into
- [`Theme`](./Theme.html), [`Color4`](./Color4.html) — colours
- [`Vertex`](./Vertex.html) — one vertex of the emitted batch

Widgets are declared inline in the frame loop; there is no retained tree. Each
frame walks the declarations and batches every panel and widget into a single
`(Array Vertex)`, which goes to the GPU as one buffer.

`gui.wgsl` is the matching shader. Rounded corners are an SDF evaluated in the
fragment shader rather than geometry, so they stay crisp at any scale.

The library itself is carp and WGSL with nothing to link against. Driving it
needs a WebGPU surface, which is what `tests/guitest.carp` demonstrates; that
file is a manual demo and needs bindings that do not live in this org.")

(save-docs Gui Context PanelState GuiRect GuiDrawCommand Theme Color4 Vertex)
; Carp's save-docs hardcodes the index filename as <title>_index.html.
; Rename to docs/index.html.
(defn main [] (System.system "mv ./docs/carp-gui_index.html ./docs/index.html"))
